1
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:05,800
Howard's capsule should be reentering

2
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:07,350
the atmosphere any minute.

3
00:00:07,350 --> 00:00:08,660
It'll be good to have him back.

4
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:11,420
The Fantastic Four reunited!

5
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:15,120
Yeah, you had a good run, fake Wolowitz.

6
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:19,040
We'll remember you with nostalgic fondness.

7
00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:23,660
The way we do the dial-up modem, the VHS tape, or...

8
00:00:23,660 --> 00:00:26,110
or Leonard's gym membership.

9
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:28,730
We're not kicking him out.

10
00:00:28,730 --> 00:00:30,810
Stuart and I have become good friends.

11
00:00:30,810 --> 00:00:32,740
Okay, one vote for, one vote against.

12
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:34,740
Leonard, you're the tiebreaker.

13
00:00:35,150 --> 00:00:36,510
I don't have a problem with stuart.

14
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:40,070
Besides, he gives us a 20% discount at his comic book store.

15
00:00:40,070 --> 00:00:42,180
Well, I don't sell my friendship that cheaply.

16
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:43,060
I can go 30.

17
00:00:43,060 --> 00:00:45,500
Welcome aboard, old chum.

18
00:00:46,490 --> 00:00:48,720
Okay, the NASA website says

19
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:51,650
Howard's final descent has begun.

20
00:00:51,720 --> 00:00:53,440
He left a boy,

21
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:57,160
he returns a boy-sized hero.

22
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:03,080
Loops, calm down!

23
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:04,800
Baruch ata Adonoy,

24
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:06,150
Eloheinu melech ha-olam,

25
00:01:06,150 --> 00:01:08,660
ha-motzi lechem min ha-aretz.

26
00:01:08,660 --> 00:01:09,570
What's that?

27
00:01:09,570 --> 00:01:12,440
The Jewish prayer for eating bread!

28
00:01:13,210 --> 00:01:16,310
We don't have one for falling out of space!

29
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:22,540
We did it!

30
00:01:22,780 --> 00:01:26,220
We're on the ground! We survived!

31
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:27,830
That was just the parachute.

32
00:01:27,830 --> 00:01:30,650
We still have another six miles to go.

33
00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:07,310
Waiting for my husband.

34
00:02:07,310 --> 00:02:08,960
That's nice.

35
00:02:09,110 --> 00:02:11,670
He's coming back from outer space.

36
00:02:12,020 --> 00:02:14,790
I think this flight's coming from Houston.

37
00:02:16,890 --> 00:02:18,860
No, I mean, he...

38
00:02:18,860 --> 00:02:20,550
Never mind.

39
00:02:21,770 --> 00:02:24,830
- There he is! - Howie! Howie!

40
00:02:28,630 --> 00:02:30,260
Whoa, thank you.

41
00:02:30,260 --> 00:02:32,430
Great to be back on Earth.

42
00:02:32,430 --> 00:02:34,920
Uh, I think they're here for me, Ringo.

43
00:02:39,090 --> 00:02:40,430
Mr. Mandel, I'm your driver.

44
00:02:40,430 --> 00:02:42,230
Oh, thanks.

45
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:45,910
That nut job was telling everybody on the plane

46
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:47,460
he's an astronaut.

47
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:50,390
I missed you so much!

48
00:02:51,810 --> 00:02:53,700
I missed you, too.

49
00:02:57,330 --> 00:02:58,480
Where are the guys?

50
00:02:58,480 --> 00:03:00,170
Oh, it's just me.

51
00:03:00,170 --> 00:03:01,120
Oh, I get it.

52
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:04,460
They're waiting back home with a big surprise party.

53
00:03:04,460 --> 00:03:06,720
Don't worry, I can act surprised.

54
00:03:09,730 --> 00:03:12,100
No, I told them they could have you tomorrow night.

55
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:14,660
Tonight, you belong to me.

56
00:03:20,650 --> 00:03:22,300
Gesundheit. You okay?

57
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:23,960
I am now that you're back.

58
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:25,340
Come on, let's go home

59
00:03:25,340 --> 00:03:27,610
so I can tear off those little pants.

60
00:03:27,610 --> 00:03:29,430
Great. Just keep in mind

61
00:03:29,430 --> 00:03:32,140
astronauts lose a lot of muscle tone in space,

62
00:03:32,140 --> 00:03:34,890
so you might have to do most of the heavy lifting.

63
00:03:36,660 --> 00:03:38,550
You know, I am very disappointed

64
00:03:38,550 --> 00:03:40,010
that I won't be able to celebrate

65
00:03:40,010 --> 00:03:41,950
Howard's accomplishment tonight.

66
00:03:41,950 --> 00:03:43,570
Me, too. But we'll see him tomorrow.

67
00:03:43,570 --> 00:03:46,650
Yes, it's just that in all the years I've known him,

68
00:03:46,650 --> 00:03:50,730
he's never had the opportunity to receive my admiration.

69
00:03:51,910 --> 00:03:53,610
I was excited to see the look on his face

70
00:03:53,610 --> 00:03:55,610
when it finally happened.

71
00:03:56,150 --> 00:03:57,930
You're unbelievable.

72
00:03:57,930 --> 00:03:59,410
I know.

73
00:04:00,130 --> 00:04:01,260
All right, Pictionary--

74
00:04:01,270 --> 00:04:02,240
what are the teams?

75
00:04:02,250 --> 00:04:03,710
How about boys versus girls?

76
00:04:03,710 --> 00:04:06,120
Oh! That hardly seems fair.

77
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:08,440
But I guess any team that I'm not on

78
00:04:08,440 --> 00:04:10,890
has a decided disadvantage.

79
00:04:11,940 --> 00:04:13,630
Once again, unbelievable.

80
00:04:13,630 --> 00:04:15,320
Yeah, once again, I know.

81
00:04:16,250 --> 00:04:18,940
All right, round one.

82
00:04:18,940 --> 00:04:20,110
Here.

83
00:04:20,110 --> 00:04:22,420
- Got it. - Okay.

84
00:04:22,420 --> 00:04:24,890
Ready, set, go.

85
00:04:26,510 --> 00:04:28,470
Uh, box?

86
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:31,340
Uh, window?

87
00:04:31,710 --> 00:04:33,070
Batman.

88
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:36,850
Batman and Robin.

89
00:04:38,970 --> 00:04:41,280
Uh, Wonder Twins plus the monkey.

90
00:04:42,690 --> 00:04:45,340
Wonder twins plus the monkey and Batman.

91
00:04:46,420 --> 00:04:48,200
A gift? Present!

92
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:49,420
Present! Yeah!

93
00:04:49,420 --> 00:04:52,090
Oh... Leonard.

94
00:04:52,090 --> 00:04:54,870
Now, how can you not get that?

95
00:04:55,530 --> 00:04:58,380
In what universe is that a present?

96
00:04:58,380 --> 00:05:00,130
It's not a present,

97
00:05:00,130 --> 00:05:02,510
it's the present. Look.

98
00:05:02,510 --> 00:05:04,070
There's you and me.

99
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:06,010
It's Penny and Amy.

100
00:05:06,010 --> 00:05:07,950
We're playing Pictionary.

101
00:05:07,950 --> 00:05:10,880
In the present.

102
00:05:14,950 --> 00:05:16,860
Oh, my God, we're gonna kill them.

103
00:05:19,380 --> 00:05:21,700
It's a quark-gluon plasma.

104
00:05:22,870 --> 00:05:23,950
No.

105
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:25,510
It's asymptotically free partons

106
00:05:25,510 --> 00:05:27,960
inside a quark-gluon plasma.

107
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:30,380
Nothing with quarks.

108
00:05:31,140 --> 00:05:32,490
It's an observational rebuttal

109
00:05:32,490 --> 00:05:35,610
of the Lambda-Cdm Model of the universe!

110
00:05:36,420 --> 00:05:37,160
No!

111
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:39,740
- It's a chocolate chip cookie! - Yes!

112
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:45,010
How could you miss that?

113
00:05:45,010 --> 00:05:47,950
Hey, if you want someone to guess "chocolate chip cookie,"

114
00:05:47,950 --> 00:05:50,670
you draw a glass of milk next to it.

115
00:05:51,630 --> 00:05:53,300
- Penny got it. - Yeah, only after

116
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:56,040
I eliminated all the obvious answers.

117
00:05:56,530 --> 00:05:58,150
You're welcome.

118
00:06:00,350 --> 00:06:03,220
Oh, uh, uh, uh, sausage.

119
00:06:03,220 --> 00:06:05,860
Uh, uh, uh, uh, bratwurst?

120
00:06:06,130 --> 00:06:08,300
Oh, oh, a hot dog.

121
00:06:09,010 --> 00:06:10,890
Penny, aren't you gonna draw something?

122
00:06:10,890 --> 00:06:13,710
Relax, we got time, this is so fun.

123
00:06:16,270 --> 00:06:17,830
There.

124
00:06:18,270 --> 00:06:19,750
A solar system.

125
00:06:19,750 --> 00:06:21,560
Uh, uh, uh,

126
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:25,100
Uh, um, unidentified flying liverwurst? I don't...

127
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:27,700
Now?

128
00:06:27,700 --> 00:06:29,340
Soon.

129
00:06:30,410 --> 00:06:31,440
Come on, Leonard,

130
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:34,580
I am spoon-feeding this to you.

131
00:06:40,660 --> 00:06:43,120
I don't know, uh...

132
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:46,160
Casper the alcoholic ghost?

133
00:06:47,620 --> 00:06:49,870
All right, that's enough.

134
00:06:52,020 --> 00:06:54,250
Uh, hand.

135
00:06:54,250 --> 00:06:56,710
- Uh, nail... polish? - Yep!

136
00:06:56,710 --> 00:07:00,480
Wait, no, no!

137
00:07:00,490 --> 00:07:02,810
The word is "Polish."

138
00:07:02,810 --> 00:07:05,790
See, look. Polish sausage.

139
00:07:05,790 --> 00:07:08,040
And the-the model of the solar system developed

140
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:11,120
by Nicolaus Copernicus, a Polish astronomer.

141
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:12,130
And then, finally,

142
00:07:12,130 --> 00:07:13,700
if that wasn't enough-- which it should've been--

143
00:07:13,700 --> 00:07:15,870
This is Madame Curie killing herself

144
00:07:15,870 --> 00:07:18,060
by discovering Radium, who,

145
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:20,220
although she was a naturalized French citizen,

146
00:07:20,220 --> 00:07:22,750
was Polish by birth!

147
00:07:25,550 --> 00:07:28,270
Excuse me, the word is "polish."

148
00:07:28,270 --> 00:07:30,670
See? Small "p."

149
00:07:35,340 --> 00:07:36,940
So it is.

150
00:07:37,450 --> 00:07:39,830
I guess we both share blame on this one.

151
00:07:43,030 --> 00:07:44,640
Bernie, you okay?

152
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:47,020
Yeah, I'll be right there.

153
00:07:52,850 --> 00:07:56,160
Did you get a sea lion while I was gone?

154
00:07:58,350 --> 00:08:00,090
It's just allergies.

155
00:08:00,090 --> 00:08:01,590
Okay.

156
00:08:02,150 --> 00:08:04,670
Took some benadryl. I'll be fine.

157
00:08:05,590 --> 00:08:06,830
So...

158
00:08:06,830 --> 00:08:08,730
Did you miss me?

159
00:08:09,830 --> 00:08:12,560
Are you kidding? Every minute of every...

160
00:08:22,820 --> 00:08:24,640
Excuse me.

161
00:08:24,670 --> 00:08:27,790
Sweetie, we don't have to do this now.

162
00:08:27,790 --> 00:08:29,870
Yes, we do.

163
00:08:34,970 --> 00:08:37,990
You left right after we got married.

164
00:08:39,050 --> 00:08:41,580
This is like our honeymoon.

165
00:08:44,290 --> 00:08:45,330
Now,

166
00:08:45,330 --> 00:08:48,120
hold on to your hat.

167
00:08:51,870 --> 00:08:52,780
You okay?

168
00:08:52,780 --> 00:08:54,310
A little dizzy.

169
00:08:54,310 --> 00:08:56,330
Must be the benadryl.

170
00:08:56,330 --> 00:08:58,470
Switch places with me.

171
00:08:58,510 --> 00:08:59,930
Okay.

172
00:09:02,810 --> 00:09:04,350
Now...

173
00:09:08,070 --> 00:09:09,780
...Kiss me!

174
00:09:21,210 --> 00:09:23,010
Bernadette?

175
00:09:25,700 --> 00:09:28,560
Bernie? Bernie?

176
00:09:29,180 --> 00:09:31,500
That was amazing.

177
00:09:35,500 --> 00:09:39,020
You made me feel things I never...

178
00:09:43,630 --> 00:09:46,880
Well, that was quick and a little gross.

179
00:09:48,170 --> 00:09:50,450
Now, I know how she feels.

180
00:09:52,900 --> 00:09:55,210
Hey, Sheldon, you're always

181
00:09:55,210 --> 00:09:57,050
full of fun little facts.

182
00:09:57,050 --> 00:09:58,170
Where did the expression

183
00:09:58,170 --> 00:10:01,040
"got your ass handed to you" come from?

184
00:10:04,170 --> 00:10:05,800
Don't know.

185
00:10:07,180 --> 00:10:09,810
I wonder if it's from, like, ancient Rome

186
00:10:09,810 --> 00:10:11,970
where they'd actually chop somebody's ass off

187
00:10:11,980 --> 00:10:14,190
and then go, "here."

188
00:10:15,780 --> 00:10:20,450
You know, to appease Loseroneous, the god of losers.

189
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:22,440
I am not a loser.

190
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:26,680
Pictionary is not a true test of any real intelligence or skill.

191
00:10:26,690 --> 00:10:28,220
Mmm, in all fairness,

192
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:30,890
Pictionary has verbal skills, visual skills.

193
00:10:30,890 --> 00:10:32,620
It's a pretty well-rounded game.

194
00:10:32,620 --> 00:10:33,700
Lot of big talk from a man

195
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:36,100
who can't draw a chocolate chip cookie.

196
00:10:36,770 --> 00:10:38,360
All right, fine, pick another game.

197
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:39,910
Amy and I will beat you at anything.

198
00:10:39,910 --> 00:10:41,510
All right.

199
00:10:41,510 --> 00:10:43,350
Let's play...

200
00:10:43,360 --> 00:10:45,490
Physics Fiesta.

201
00:10:46,710 --> 00:10:48,540
Oh, come on, what is that?

202
00:10:48,540 --> 00:10:50,450
It's a game that I just invented,

203
00:10:50,450 --> 00:10:55,410
in which the participants answer physics questions in remedial Spanish.

204
00:10:56,580 --> 00:10:59,870
Donde esta el boson de higgs?

205
00:11:00,130 --> 00:11:03,060
En el acelerador de particulares.

206
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:06,520
Bueno, mi amigo.

207
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:11,830
No, no, we're not playing some dumb made-up game.

208
00:11:11,830 --> 00:11:13,730
All games are made up.

209
00:11:13,730 --> 00:11:15,490
They're not found in nature.

210
00:11:15,490 --> 00:11:17,660
You don't just dig in the ground, come across

211
00:11:17,660 --> 00:11:20,450
a rich vein of rock'em sock'em robots.

212
00:11:21,330 --> 00:11:22,740
Just pick another game.

213
00:11:22,740 --> 00:11:24,240
Why don't we do something athletic

214
00:11:24,240 --> 00:11:27,220
like go over to the university pool and play water polo?

215
00:11:27,220 --> 00:11:29,700
No good-- Sheldon doesn't float.

216
00:11:30,460 --> 00:11:31,490
That is true.

217
00:11:31,490 --> 00:11:33,750
I have a higher than normal body density.

218
00:11:33,750 --> 00:11:36,580
If I run too deep a bath, I drown.

219
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:38,890
All right, let's keep it simple.

220
00:11:38,890 --> 00:11:39,750
How about darts?

221
00:11:39,750 --> 00:11:41,290
Oh, that's not fair either.

222
00:11:41,290 --> 00:11:41,960
Why not?

223
00:11:41,960 --> 00:11:43,790
Darts is a bar game.

224
00:11:43,790 --> 00:11:48,040
You've been frequenting drinking establishments since you were of legal age.

225
00:11:48,690 --> 00:11:51,270
Yeah, that's when it started.

226
00:11:52,410 --> 00:11:54,900
Well, regardless, she has a distinct advantage

227
00:11:54,900 --> 00:11:56,550
in all tavern- based competitions.

228
00:11:56,550 --> 00:11:58,860
Pool, beer pong, wet T-shirt contests--

229
00:11:58,860 --> 00:12:00,010
they're all out.

230
00:12:00,020 --> 00:12:01,600
Okay.

231
00:12:01,600 --> 00:12:02,930
Just for the record,

232
00:12:02,930 --> 00:12:05,260
I have never entered a wet T-shirt contest.

233
00:12:05,270 --> 00:12:07,810
I've won a few, but that's just because I spill when I'm drunk,

234
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:09,420
So...

235
00:12:10,510 --> 00:12:12,480
We could go to the cadaver lab at UCLA

236
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:14,640
and play real-life operation.

237
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:18,900
- No. - I don't think so.

238
00:12:18,900 --> 00:12:21,000
Are you sure? I mean, the nose doesn't light up,

239
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,120
but if the corpse is fresh enough,

240
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:24,810
sometimes you can get the leg to jerk.

241
00:12:28,220 --> 00:12:30,120
Hey, Ma, twinkle, twinkle,

242
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:32,650
your little star is home!

243
00:12:34,010 --> 00:12:36,970
Ma, the chain's on the door!

244
00:12:37,050 --> 00:12:38,000
Howard?

245
00:12:38,010 --> 00:12:41,800
I thought I wasn't going to see you till tomorrow!

246
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:44,050
Yeah, well, Bernie's not feeling well,

247
00:12:44,050 --> 00:12:45,860
so I thought I'd stop by,

248
00:12:45,860 --> 00:12:48,660
tell you about the greatest adventure of my life,

249
00:12:48,660 --> 00:12:50,880
see if you can make me feel bad about it.

250
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:56,640
Uh, uh, okay, hold on, I'm not decent!

251
00:12:56,680 --> 00:12:58,420
All right.

252
00:12:58,800 --> 00:13:00,630
Woman hasn't tied her robe in 20 years.

253
00:13:00,630 --> 00:13:02,670
Suddenly she's not decent?

254
00:13:02,830 --> 00:13:06,590
You want me to hide in the closet or go out the back?!

255
00:13:07,780 --> 00:13:10,690
Shh, you need to whisper.

256
00:13:10,690 --> 00:13:12,300
Ma, who is in there?

257
00:13:12,310 --> 00:13:15,360
Uh, nobody! The TV is on!

258
00:13:15,650 --> 00:13:17,130
I only got one sock.

259
00:13:17,140 --> 00:13:19,520
Where's my other sock?

260
00:13:19,730 --> 00:13:20,660
Who is that?

261
00:13:20,660 --> 00:13:22,290
I told you, it's the TV.

262
00:13:22,290 --> 00:13:25,810
Jay Leno lost a sock; it's hilarious.

263
00:13:26,790 --> 00:13:29,570
If you're busy, I can come back.

264
00:13:29,570 --> 00:13:31,100
Just give me a second!

265
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:33,070
Go, go, go, go.

266
00:13:42,970 --> 00:13:44,230
Dr. Schneider?

267
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:47,110
Oh, hello, Howard.

268
00:13:48,460 --> 00:13:49,920
What are you doing here?

269
00:13:49,930 --> 00:13:52,820
Um, house call.

270
00:13:53,710 --> 00:13:55,750
You're a dentist.

271
00:13:56,660 --> 00:13:59,200
Yes, yes, I am.

272
00:13:59,200 --> 00:14:02,040
I think he's on to us!

273
00:14:07,550 --> 00:14:09,830
Okay, glasses off.

274
00:14:09,830 --> 00:14:11,720
Find Waldo.

275
00:14:17,010 --> 00:14:18,920
Hurry up, find him, find him.

276
00:14:18,920 --> 00:14:20,540
I'm trying! Don't yell at me!

277
00:14:20,540 --> 00:14:22,710
For goodness' sake, he's wearing a hat, glasses,

278
00:14:22,710 --> 00:14:23,870
and a red striped shirt.

279
00:14:23,870 --> 00:14:26,040
I know what he looks like.

280
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:27,100
Oh, there he is, I got him.

281
00:14:27,100 --> 00:14:29,910
Yes, we win again!

282
00:14:30,020 --> 00:14:31,830
How could you not find him?

283
00:14:31,830 --> 00:14:34,490
Because he's hard to find.

284
00:14:34,500 --> 00:14:35,480
If he was easy to find,

285
00:14:35,480 --> 00:14:38,160
The books would be called There's Waldo.

286
00:14:43,720 --> 00:14:45,470
that's one minute.

287
00:14:48,420 --> 00:14:50,060
Long division, long division.

288
00:14:50,060 --> 00:14:51,670
Go, go, go.

289
00:14:51,790 --> 00:14:53,710
Remember, show your work.

290
00:14:55,770 --> 00:14:56,970
I'm okay.

291
00:14:56,970 --> 00:14:58,560
I'm okay.

292
00:15:02,180 --> 00:15:03,840
I'm not okay.

293
00:15:04,490 --> 00:15:06,660
Get up, we can't lose in math.

294
00:15:06,660 --> 00:15:08,950
- 37! - Yes!

295
00:15:10,620 --> 00:15:12,890
Ready, set, wrestle.

296
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:16,490
One, two, three, pin.

297
00:15:18,940 --> 00:15:20,440
Stop that.

298
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:23,190
Amy, do something.

299
00:15:23,190 --> 00:15:24,530
Amy, help.

300
00:15:24,530 --> 00:15:27,250
Amy, stop that.

301
00:15:27,250 --> 00:15:30,040
Amy, Penny, both of you, stop it.

302
00:15:33,520 --> 00:15:35,300
One to beam aboard?

303
00:15:35,350 --> 00:15:38,210
Oh, my God, you're back.

304
00:15:38,400 --> 00:15:39,540
Oh, look at you.

305
00:15:39,550 --> 00:15:41,510
You, you look like you grew.

306
00:15:41,510 --> 00:15:43,030
Yeah.

307
00:15:44,270 --> 00:15:46,640
The lack of gravity did decompress my spine,

308
00:15:46,640 --> 00:15:48,930
so I'm like an inch and a half taller.

309
00:15:49,680 --> 00:15:51,640
I'm going to the DMV tomorrow to get my license changed

310
00:15:51,640 --> 00:15:53,400
before I shrink back.

311
00:15:53,440 --> 00:15:55,370
Oh, uh, come in, come in.

312
00:15:55,370 --> 00:15:57,180
Oh, I, uh, I didn't think I was going to get

313
00:15:57,180 --> 00:15:58,710
to see you until tomorrow.

314
00:15:58,710 --> 00:16:01,970
Yeah, well, Bernadette's a little under the weather

315
00:16:01,970 --> 00:16:05,360
and my mom's kind of under my dentist.

316
00:16:06,490 --> 00:16:09,370
Wait, your, your mother is sleeping with your dentist?

317
00:16:09,370 --> 00:16:10,300
Former dentist.

318
00:16:10,310 --> 00:16:13,260
I need a new one now that I know where his hands have been.

319
00:16:14,880 --> 00:16:17,710
So you're wandering all around by yourself?

320
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:19,170
That's not the kind of hero's welcome

321
00:16:19,170 --> 00:16:20,650
an astronaut should come home to.

322
00:16:20,650 --> 00:16:23,580
It's okay, you know, we space cowboys

323
00:16:23,580 --> 00:16:27,340
don't do what we do for glory and fame.

324
00:16:27,340 --> 00:16:31,260
We leave that to your rock stars and your athletes

325
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:33,430
and your Howie Mandels.

326
00:16:35,890 --> 00:16:38,800
Oh, hey, man, welcome back.

327
00:16:38,800 --> 00:16:40,910
Oh, Stuart, thanks.

328
00:16:40,910 --> 00:16:41,900
What are you doing here?

329
00:16:41,900 --> 00:16:43,780
I, I kind of live here now.

330
00:16:43,780 --> 00:16:45,690
Just until he gets back on his feet,

331
00:16:45,690 --> 00:16:46,860
which are looking pretty good

332
00:16:46,860 --> 00:16:49,770
in the boots I bought him for his birthday.

333
00:16:52,800 --> 00:16:55,680
Ah, he's spoiling me and I love it.

334
00:16:57,320 --> 00:17:01,220
Wow, so you guys are like buds now?

335
00:17:01,220 --> 00:17:03,230
Oh, yeah, we hang out all the time.

336
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:04,760
Plus, he doesn't have a girlfriend,

337
00:17:04,760 --> 00:17:05,700
I don't have a girlfriend.

338
00:17:05,700 --> 00:17:07,710
It's like we both had these holes in our lives,

339
00:17:07,710 --> 00:17:10,070
but now we fill each other's holes.

340
00:17:17,250 --> 00:17:21,550
That sounds a little funny to an American ear.

341
00:17:21,860 --> 00:17:24,550
- Which part? - Just all of it.

342
00:17:26,320 --> 00:17:29,480
Okay, so w-what do you guys got going on tonight?

343
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:33,100
Raj is taking me to the sound of music sing-along.

344
00:17:33,470 --> 00:17:34,760
Sound of music sing-along?

345
00:17:34,760 --> 00:17:37,800
That used to be our thing, but that's cool.

346
00:17:37,800 --> 00:17:39,630
Oh, Howard, it's still our thing.

347
00:17:39,630 --> 00:17:42,040
Come with us, we'll, we'll get you a scalped ticket.

348
00:17:42,040 --> 00:17:44,730
So I'd be sitting by myself?

349
00:17:44,730 --> 00:17:45,600
We'll switch.

350
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:47,440
You'll come sit with me after intermission.

351
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:51,060
So I-I-I'd be sitting by myself during "Edelweiss"?

352
00:17:52,050 --> 00:17:55,280
No, no, you guys go. Have fun.

353
00:17:55,360 --> 00:17:57,120
Okay, uh, will I get to see you tomorrow?

354
00:17:57,130 --> 00:17:58,850
Absolutely. See you, Stuart.

355
00:17:58,850 --> 00:18:00,500
Yeah, yeah.

356
00:18:02,120 --> 00:18:03,740
Is he taller?

357
00:18:06,850 --> 00:18:09,810
At least my mother made her boyfriend climb out the window.

358
00:18:13,050 --> 00:18:17,070
All right, standard state fair pie-eating contest rules are:

359
00:18:17,070 --> 00:18:20,580
No hands, first one to clean the pan wins.

360
00:18:21,290 --> 00:18:23,000
On the count of three.

361
00:18:23,030 --> 00:18:26,670
- One, two... - Wait.

362
00:18:28,820 --> 00:18:30,930
I'm a little concerned.

363
00:18:30,930 --> 00:18:33,310
Blueberries are rich in antioxidants.

364
00:18:33,310 --> 00:18:34,290
So?

365
00:18:34,290 --> 00:18:36,230
So, with all those antioxidants,

366
00:18:36,230 --> 00:18:38,560
what if I run out of oxidants?

367
00:18:41,550 --> 00:18:44,910
Sheldon, we haven't won a game all night.

368
00:18:45,410 --> 00:18:47,020
Now, you either stick your face in that pie

369
00:18:47,020 --> 00:18:49,530
or I'm gonna stick that pie in your face.

370
00:18:52,940 --> 00:18:54,540
That's rude.

371
00:18:55,850 --> 00:19:00,490
One, two, three, eat.

372
00:19:08,980 --> 00:19:11,230
Hey, guys, guess who's back from space.

373
00:19:11,230 --> 00:19:13,420
Not now!

374
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:20,430
Oh, ow, blueberry in my nose,

375
00:19:20,430 --> 00:19:22,330
blueberry in my nose!

376
00:19:22,850 --> 00:19:25,040
Snort it down and keep eating!

377
00:19:36,500 --> 00:19:38,550
You look familiar.

378
00:19:38,660 --> 00:19:40,430
I don't think so.

379
00:19:40,470 --> 00:19:43,960
Yeah, I just saw you on the news.

380
00:19:43,960 --> 00:19:45,600
You're an astronaut.

381
00:19:45,600 --> 00:19:46,810
Yes.

382
00:19:46,810 --> 00:19:48,230
Yes, I am.

383
00:19:48,230 --> 00:19:50,030
Good for you.

384
00:19:50,250 --> 00:19:52,410
How about a piece of cheesecake on the house?

385
00:19:52,410 --> 00:19:54,340
Oh, thank you so much.

386
00:19:54,350 --> 00:19:55,800
I've been having the worst night.

387
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:58,220
I just got back, and my friends don't care,

388
00:19:58,220 --> 00:19:59,150
my wife's sick, I went to my mom...

389
00:19:59,150 --> 00:20:01,500
You want the cheesecake or not?

390
00:20:04,310 --> 00:20:05,880
Yes, please.

391
00:20:09,560 --> 00:20:12,680
* And I think it's gonna be a long, long time *

392
00:20:12,680 --> 00:20:16,110
* till touchdown brings me 'round again to find *

393
00:20:16,110 --> 00:20:18,940
* I'm not the man they think I am at home *

394
00:20:20,500 --> 00:20:22,700
* I'm a rocket man. *

395
00:20:29,340 --> 00:20:30,900
Perfect.

